WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:05.010
Despite the saturation of comic based stories
on screen, superhero fatigue has apparently

00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:09.650
yet to set in with audiences, as Avengers:
Infinity War cleaned up at the box office

00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:11.299
with a record breaking take.

00:00:11.299 --> 00:00:14.740
But just because Earth's mightiest heroes
are still as popular as ever, that doesn't

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:16.450
mean they're all safe from elimination.

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:20.650
2018 has already proven to be pretty intense
when it comes to central characters biting

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:25.030
the dust, and already this year, we have a
large body count of superheroes stacking up.

00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:26.850
"I hope they remember you."

00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:30.769
Sure, a lot of them may be back sooner than
later, but for now, let's take a moment to

00:00:30.769 --> 00:00:35.989
mourn those we've lost across the comics universe,
from the page to the small screen to the theater.

00:00:35.989 --> 00:00:38.260
Spoilers ahead!

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:39.260
Clayface

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:42.989
It might not make sense at first to see the
name of one of Batman's signature villains

00:00:42.989 --> 00:00:47.289
on a list of fallen superheroes, but Basil
Karlo had recently taken steps to change his

00:00:47.289 --> 00:00:49.690
ways and make up for his many wrongs.

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:53.090
Batman was even attempting to recruit him
into the ranks of the Gotham Knights, but

00:00:53.090 --> 00:00:58.329
toward the end of the Fall of the Batmen storyline,
Clayface went wild and smashed through Gotham,

00:00:58.329 --> 00:00:59.809
destroying everything in his path.

00:00:59.809 --> 00:01:03.420
While most of the team tried to find a non
lethal way to stop their budding teammate's

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:08.140
rampage, Batwoman was given a gun designed
to kill Clayface by her father Colonel Kane.

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:13.640
Detective Comics #973 ended with Batwoman
blasting Basil Karlo through the skull.

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:17.640
And just in case it wasn't clear that this
wasn't some cliffhanger, Dr. October confirmed

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:21.920
his death in the following issue, and Batwoman
was ejected from the Gotham Knights as a result

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:23.610
of her act.

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:25.720
The Mighty Thor and Mjolnir

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:29.940
For years, Jane Foster has been carrying the
mantle and weapon of Thor, but all that world

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:33.159
saving has been slowly but surely taking its
toll on her.

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:37.310
Foster was suffering from cancer when she
took up Mjolnir, and eventually, she learned

00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:41.950
that every time she transformed into the hero,
she undid all of her chemotherapy treatment.

00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:45.690
As more people in her life learned of this,
they grew more adamant that she stop turning

00:01:45.690 --> 00:01:49.049
into Thor and let the rest of the world's
heroes do the heavy lifting.

00:01:49.049 --> 00:01:52.340
When the Mangog was unleashed on Asgardia,
though, she had to step in.

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:58.219
In Mighty Thor #705, Thor used unbreakable
chains to wrap Mjolnir and Mangog, and hurled

00:01:58.219 --> 00:01:59.770
the both of them into the Sun.

00:01:59.770 --> 00:02:02.430
Mjolnir was destroyed, and Mangog was imprisoned.

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:06.060
Without Mjolnir, Thor reverted back to Jane
Foster and died.

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:10.260
Ultimately, the human version of herself would
survive thanks to some heavenly intervention,

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:14.960
but her version of Thor was done for, alongside
the trusty weapon.

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:16.000
Ghost Rider

00:02:16.390 --> 00:02:21.540
Johnny Blaze went out in a blaze of intentional
glory during Marvel's mini event, Damnation.

00:02:21.550 --> 00:02:25.950
Mephisto seized on an opportunity to try and
bring hell to Earth, by way of the City of

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:26.950
Sin, Las Vegas.

00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:30.980
While Doctor Strange resisted the effort,
Wong cobbled together a makeshift Midnight

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:35.920
Sons team that included Johnny Blaze, Marvel's
original motorcycle riding Ghost Rider.

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:40.990
In Doctor Strange: Damnation #3, Blaze confronted
Mephisto, but unimpressed with his old enemy's

00:02:40.990 --> 00:02:45.550
bravado, Mephisto snuffed out the flame of
Johnny's skull, lifting the Ghost Rider curse

00:02:45.550 --> 00:02:46.550
from him.

00:02:46.550 --> 00:02:50.870
Then, with Blaze's powers gone, Mephisto send
him to hell alongside his "dark passenger."

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:55.280
But with the throne unguarded, Blaze gathered
an assortment of D list supervillains to join

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:59.930
forces and stage a revolution to use the power
of the underworld to help Strange and his

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:05.070
other allies, proving that even death isn't
the end for some heroes.

00:03:05.070 --> 00:03:06.070
Rip Hunter

00:03:06.070 --> 00:03:10.840
In the season 3 finale of Legends of Tomorrow,
the time hopping team lost the guy who brought

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:13.540
them all together: the former Time Master
Rip Hunter.

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:17.870
Hunter perishes while trying to save his friends
from the demon Mallus by detonating a time

00:03:17.870 --> 00:03:20.180
core to give the rest of the Legends time
to escape.

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:24.850
And while the explosion took Hunter out completely,
it only weakened his demonic enemy.

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:27.730
Hunter wasn't alone in meeting his fate in
the season finale.

00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:33.790
The otherwise nefarious Damien Darhk sacrificed
himself to Mallus to save his daughter Nora.

00:03:33.790 --> 00:03:35.150
Ralph Dibny

00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:39.400
The Flash's villain Clifford DeVoe, a.k.a
the Thinker, has been racking up a large body

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:43.680
count in the show's fourth season by absorbing
the powers of Central City's metas.

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:48.870
Perhaps the most devastating loss of all is
Ralph Dibny, a.k.a. DC's Elongated Man.

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:53.310
Ralph had the misfortune to be standing next
to DeVoe after he was captured by Team Flash.

00:03:53.310 --> 00:03:56.980
DeVoe freed himself, and used his powers on
Dibny, ending his life.

00:03:56.980 --> 00:03:57.980
Is he gone for good?

00:03:57.980 --> 00:04:03.080
Well, The Flash does have a tendency to bring
back the departed, so time will tell.

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:04.080
Heimdall

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:08.010
Avengers: Infinity War brought a lot of loss
to the Marvel Cinematic Universe, and the

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:11.540
first of its victims was one of the last Asgardians:
Heimdall.

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:15.120
After helping to rescue the Asgardians at
the end of Thor: Ragnarok, Heimdall is on

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:18.450
board the refugee ship when Thanos and his
Black Order attack.

00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:22.180
Although he's already badly injured, Heimdall
uses the last of his strength to activate

00:04:22.180 --> 00:04:26.280
the Bifrost and send the unconscious Hulk
to Earth, and it's a decision that costs him

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:29.600
his life, possibly forever.

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:30.650
Loki

00:04:30.650 --> 00:04:35.440
Some fans might have trouble believing Loki
has finally met his maker for good this time,

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:38.870
considering he's "died" twice already in the
first two Thor films.

00:04:38.870 --> 00:04:41.120
"I wish I could trust you."

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:45.100
But Infinity War might have actually brought
the God of Mischief down once and for all.

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:49.180
After Thanos and the Black Order board the
refugee ship, Loki initially seems unwilling

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:50.790
to give up the Tesseract.

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:54.060
Unwilling to watch his brother suffer at the
hands of Thanos, he gives in and gives the

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:55.650
bad guy what he wants.

00:04:55.650 --> 00:04:59.160
Loki tricks everyone into thinking he wants
to join Thanos in his search for the remaining

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:02.500
Infinity Stones… until he lunges at Thanos,
dagger in hand.

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:06.180
He stops Loki's attack easily, and chokes
the life out of him.

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:09.570
Considering the countless innocents who died
at Loki's hands in the first Avengers, not

00:05:09.570 --> 00:05:13.690
to mention the attempted genocide of his own
race, it could be argued that Loki's death

00:05:13.690 --> 00:05:16.910
belongs nowhere near a list of fallen superheroes.

00:05:16.910 --> 00:05:20.450
However, considering his actions at the end
of Ragnarok and beyond, while the guy might

00:05:20.450 --> 00:05:25.390
not have been perfect, he clearly deserves
to be considered more than just a supervillain.

00:05:25.390 --> 00:05:26.890
Gamora

00:05:26.890 --> 00:05:30.770
Of all the death doled out by Thanos in Avengers:
Infinity War, the only one that he showed

00:05:30.770 --> 00:05:34.480
any remorse for was the sacrifice of his adoptive
daughter Gamora.

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:38.620
Gamora is forced to reveal the location of
the Soul Stone to Thanos when he threatens

00:05:38.620 --> 00:05:41.300
to continue torturing the imprisoned Nebula.

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:45.360
She leads Thanos to the planet Vormir, where
the two of them are met by the ghostly apparition

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:46.360
of the Red Skull.

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:49.930
The Skull explains to Thanos that in order
to gain the Soul Stone, he must sacrifice

00:05:49.930 --> 00:05:51.170
that which he loves most.

00:05:51.170 --> 00:05:55.050
Although Gamora thinks he's lost because she
believes he loves nothing, he tearfully throws

00:05:55.050 --> 00:05:59.480
her over the rocky precipice, and we see her
corpse on the ground below before Thanos claims

00:05:59.480 --> 00:06:01.520
his prize.

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:02.520
Vision

00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:06.300
As a character whose very life presumably
depends upon keeping hold of one of the Infinity

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:09.850
Stones, the Vision is constantly threatened
with death in Avengers: Infinity War.

00:06:09.850 --> 00:06:14.080
He comes dangerously close to getting taken
out the first time the Black Order attacks,

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:17.150
but he's saved by the timely intervention
of a few friendly heroes.

00:06:17.150 --> 00:06:21.250
Once he learns of Thanos' plans, Vision insists
the only choice is to let Scarlet Witch use

00:06:21.250 --> 00:06:23.150
her powers to destroy the Mind Stone.

00:06:23.150 --> 00:06:27.680
Captain America brings the team to Wakanda
to see if Shuri can save Vision and the universe,

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:30.400
but once Thanos arrives in Wakanda, it's too
late.

00:06:30.400 --> 00:06:34.560
Scarlet Witch destroys the Mind Stone, taking
out Vision in the process, but Thanos uses

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:38.610
the powers of the Time Stone to put Vision
and the Mind Stone back together, then rips

00:06:38.610 --> 00:06:42.870
the stone from Vision's head, and leaving
him lifeless once again.

00:06:42.870 --> 00:06:44.090
Ashes to ashes

00:06:44.090 --> 00:06:47.410
If you're watching this, you already know
that Infinity War still ended with a very

00:06:47.410 --> 00:06:48.730
dark cliffhanger.

00:06:48.730 --> 00:06:52.840
One of the comics that heavily influenced
the movie was the 1991 mini series Infinity

00:06:52.840 --> 00:06:53.840
Gauntlet.

00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:58.120
In the source material, the story begins when
Thanos already has all six Infinity Gems,

00:06:58.120 --> 00:07:02.700
and with a snap of his fingers, simply eliminates
half the sentient beings in the universe,

00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:05.210
including a huge chunk of Earth's superhero
ranks.

00:07:05.210 --> 00:07:09.561
Avengers: Infinity War saves this moment for
the end, and it's devastating not only to

00:07:09.561 --> 00:07:13.520
the civilian populace of the universe, but
the ranks of the Avengers and their allies.

00:07:13.520 --> 00:07:17.669
Needless to say, the Russo brothers' portrayal
of the event is much more horrific than the

00:07:17.669 --> 00:07:18.669
source material.

00:07:18.669 --> 00:07:22.930
In Infinity War, they feel what's coming before
it hits, and they're slowly erased, inch by

00:07:22.930 --> 00:07:24.639
inch, until there's nothing left.

00:07:24.639 --> 00:07:29.180
By the time the credits roll we see Bucky,
Black Panther, Scarlet Witch, Falcon, Drax,

00:07:29.180 --> 00:07:35.150
Doctor Strange, Spider Man, Star Lord, Mantis,
Groot, Nick Fury, and Maria Hill all get erased

00:07:35.150 --> 00:07:37.150
from the canvas of reality.

00:07:37.150 --> 00:07:39.950
Considering that there are already confirmed
sequels in the works for Guardians of the

00:07:39.950 --> 00:07:44.510
Galaxy, Black Panther, and Spider Man, it's
a safe bet that not all of these dusty deaths

00:07:44.510 --> 00:07:45.510
will stick.

00:07:45.510 --> 00:07:49.790
But if they do get reversed, it likely won't
be until next year's Avengers sequel, and

00:07:49.790 --> 00:07:52.620
we won't know until then who will come back
and who won't.

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:54.560
Thanks for watching!

00:07:54.560 --> 00:07:57.120
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:07:57.120 --> 00:07:59.300
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

